WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.580
Here is a cubic: x cubed minus six x squared
plus eleven x minus six equals nought.

2
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.600
Try x equals one.

3
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:13.490
One, minus six, plus eleven, minus six.

4
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:14.640
That's nought.

5
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.290
One root, found in seconds.

6
00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.320
Do you keep guessing
numbers until two more work?

7
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.490
Or is there a way to find
them without blind guessing?

8
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:27.150
Once you have one easy root,
how do the other two follow?

9
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.670
In this mission, you'll
learn the factor theorem,

10
00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:33.250
and how to test likely roots
of a polynomial quickly.

11
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.770
Then you'll practise algebraic division, by
long division or by comparing coefficients.

12
00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.920
Your mission: show how the other
two roots follow from the easy one.
